  "necessary_adaptations": [
    {
      "reason": "Go process boundary",
      "details": "Original bound Python func becomes declared handler string and actual current Go SDK RPC. async metadata explicitly represents inspect.iscoroutinefunction; no Python runtime or emulation system. Only supported JSON declaration data crosses process boundary; no arbitrary Python callable/object/exception repr compatibility is claimed."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Existing typed Go trigger contract",
      "details": "Calendar/timezone/interval/date/jitter are normalized into schedule.Spec; ordinary kwargs and business input remain separate. Existing Go spec expects explicit IANA timezone. Constructor dictionaries from Python are ported by author into this spec; arbitrary Python trigger objects cannot be shared. Go time.Duration bounds apply to seconds/grace/jitter representability; out-of-range is explicit error rather than overflow."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Random generator runtime",
      "details": "uniform jitter formula, microsecond rounding, interval anchoring and cron clipping match controlled dependency oracle; Go RNG stream is not CPython MT stream."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Existing host integration",
      "details": "Single-user application session/origin/API auth and native JSON envelope retained; fixed compatible service routes provided. Chinese host identity localization supplies source aliases, without adding a new global locale engine. SDK errors are safe Go diagnostics with existing system.error reporting, not unrestricted Python traceback strings."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Go worker lifecycle",
      "details": "Actual reload/stop invalidates old RPC capability generation and cancels real held worker HTTP. Pure host logical ID progress/finish behavior retains fixed source old-completion/new-job effect. Progress and clocks are in-memory, rebuilt from current config after restart, with no durable replay framework."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Scoped cache region",
      "details": "The plugin service progress uses fixed 1024/24h TLRU policy within this host service map. It does not add unrelated global cache/other business progress systems."
    }
  ],
